# .publicignore — manifest for scripts/sync-public-mirror.ps1
#
# Patterns here are EXCLUDED from the public mirror at
# https://github.com/keithrlucier/toast-notification.
#
# Syntax mirrors .gitignore (glob patterns, leading "!" for explicit
# inclusions). The sync script applies BOTH .gitignore AND this file when
# copying from the private repo into the public worktree.
#
# When you add a new internal doc / artifact / config, add the pattern here.
# When you genuinely want a private path to ship publicly, add a "!pattern"
# inclusion below.
#
# Run `.\scripts\sync-public-mirror.ps1 -Tag <vN.x.y> -DryRun` after editing
# this file to see what the public worktree would look like.


# === Internal operational docs ===
# Anything under Docs/ToastRevival/ is internal milestone/handoff/evidence
# tracking and never ships publicly. PUBLIC-MIRROR.md documents the team's
# internal sync workflow and stays private — public users do not need to know
# how we generate the public mirror.
Docs/ToastRevival/
Docs/PUBLIC-MIRROR.md

# Code-review ledger and rotated history — internal QA artifacts. Reference
# customer hostnames, internal finding IDs, file:line evidence trails.
REVIEW_LEDGER.md
Docs/review_history/
docs/review_history/

# Keep the public-facing operator doc at Docs/ root explicitly.
!Docs/rollyourown.md

# Asset directories with private screenshots, SSH keys, internal-only images.
Docs/Assets/

# Team memory + session state (Claude/Codex/etc.).
.docpro/
.claude/

# === Production infrastructure ===
# nginx configs, systemd units, certbot configs — all reference production
# hosts and private network details. Self-hosters do not need these and they
# leak prod topology.
infrastructure/

# === Internal manifest ===
# This file itself: it documents the team's public-mirror sanitization
# strategy and references internal patterns. Operators do not need it.
.publicignore

# Build artifacts that should never reach a public repo.
publish/
artifacts/
dist/
src/ToastRevival.Dashboard/dist/

# Test-output directories.
TestResults/
**/TestResults/

# Local dev / IDE / OS dross that .gitignore also handles, listed here for
# defensive sync-time exclusion in case a file slipped past .gitignore.
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
.idea/
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets / signing material (defense-in-depth alongside .gitignore).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pvk
*.spc
.github-pat

# === Backend / framework debris ===
bin/
obj/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# === Frontend debris ===
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
src/ToastRevival.Dashboard/.eslintcache

# === Velopack / Squirrel release feeds ===
# Self-hosters build their own releases; the SaaS feed isn't useful to them
# and the directory carries our signing artifacts when populated.
releases/
**/releases/

# === Top-level files that are private ===
# Local dev workspace file with absolute paths.
toast-docpro.code-workspace
